### Chat lifecycle (ChatController, /rest/v1)
### Run against the "dev" environment (http-client.env.json) -> host = http://localhost:8085
### No auth required - /rest/** is permitAll (see ResourceServerConfig).

@conversationId = {{$uuid}}
# http://localhost:8080/rest/v1/ai-orchestrator/lp/chat?conversationId=ff0aab98-9a64-4391-bbb7-ac556c1a80bf
### 1. Case#1 - user is redirected to the AI Assistant from LP HOME.
### Creates a new chat and stores the user's first question.
POST {{host}}/rest/v1/lp/chat?conversationId={{conversationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Hello, what can you help me with?"
}

###

### 2. Rename the chat created above.
POST {{host}}/rest/v1/chat/name?conversationId={{conversationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newName": "Getting started with TI Assistant"
}

###

### 3. Delete the chat (and its questions) created above.
DELETE {{host}}/rest/v1/chat?conversationId={{conversationId}}

###
